// Long Time Way - the exploration theme from Giten Megami Tensei (1995),
// reimagined. The original is a General MIDI file; this keeps its notes,
// its form and its mood and changes what plays them.
//
// What the original is. D minor, 120 beats a minute, and almost nothing
// happening, on purpose - it is music for walking. Everything rests on one
// figure: a bass in unbroken sixteenths, D A D C D A F G A C D C and then
// either A C G A or F E D C, alternating bar by bar, for all eighty bars.
// Over it, very slowly:
//
//   roots   a synth bass holds a root for four bars at a time, D A Bb C -
//           i, v, bVI, bVII, the aeolian loop that every long road in a
//           game is paved with. The figure never changes to follow it, so
//           over Bb and C it rubs, which is most of the mood. From the
//           second statement the same roots gallop - an eighth and two
//           sixteenths on every beat - and that, with the kit, is the whole
//           of the lift.
//   voices  a choir holds the chords, voiced low: D F A D, E G C over A
//           (an Am7 with the root in the bass), D F Bb, and E A C over C.
//   melody  a bowed pad, first as a single held D, then D F, then D F A,
//           then two voices a third apart moving by step, one whole note a
//           bar: G F G F over D, E F G E over A, A F G A over Bb, G F E G
//           over C. Over D that is the ninth and the eleventh, never the
//           triad - the melody floats over the chord rather than sitting in
//           it. It is played three times.
//   drums   nothing for forty bars, then four bars of sixteenth hats
//           alone over a held D and F, a snare fill, and a plain backbeat -
//           kick on 1 and 3, snare on 2 and 4 - with a fill every fourth
//           bar, arriving with the second statement and the gallop.
//
// What changes. The sounds, and only as far as the mood allows:
//
//   The figure is three instruments at once. A plucked upright - the
//   original's acoustic bass, and the piece's beat until the drums come -
//   with plucked cellos an octave above it, which is how an orchestra makes
//   a bass line heard: the double bass is the floor, the cello the edge.
//   And under both Tide, a
//   synth bass whose filter ticks open on every sixteenth and whose
//   dynamics are the filter, so the intro's crescendo is the line
//   brightening under the pluck, the way a modern track builds on one
//   figure. The roots are Drift, a bass that swells in rather
//   than being struck, so a chord change arrives like a change of light.
//
//   The melody is on real string sections - first violins on the upper
//   voice, violas on the lower - with a supersaw pad behind the violins,
//   so it is both bowed and synthetic, which is what the original's
//   "bowed pad" patch was reaching for. The choir is a sampled choir, with
//   the same pad behind it.
//
//   The kit is acoustic, the Salamander kit, and it keeps the original's
//   patience and its beat: nothing until the melody's first statement is
//   ending, then the hats alone for four bars, then the backbeat and its
//   fills as written. The hats are the kit's second part, `hats`, so they
//   have a fader of their own and sit under the backbeat the way a mixed
//   record's hats do. The shaker and the crashes are a third, `fx`, on
//   Circuit, a kit sfizz synthesizes.
//   The roots' gallop is Tide, the ostinato's own synth bass, as a part of
//   its own; Drift cannot gallop, it has no attack. Before the drums, a
//   shaker, quietly, from the moment the choir arrives.
//
//   The high Bb that turns into the melody - the original's one gesture, a
//   bowed synth wrenched up a tone on the pitch wheel and let sag back -
//   gets a voice of its own, Keen, a crying synth lead that can bend, and
//   plays the 1995 bend as it was written.
//
//   The original drenches everything in reverb (every channel sends 110 of
//   127, the drums 120), and a synth kit next to a sampled choir sounds as
//   if it is in another building unless it has air of its own; so this ensemble
//   puts the kit in the hall and sends everything more.
//
//   One line is new: in the third statement the upper voice of the melody
//   goes up an octave. A third time through the same sixteen bars needs
//   something to be different; that is all it gets. (A bright pluck on
//   the chord used to join it, and was cut: it made the end overwhelming.)
//
// Form. Everything up to the drums plays once: the intro, the choir, the
// Bb that sets out, the first statement and the four bars of hats. That is
// the start of the journey, and it is never revisited. The loop is the
// journey itself - the second and third statements, with the gallop and
// the kit, bars 45 to 76 of the original. `home` and `end` are the way out.

title: Long Time Way
ensemble: wayfarer
parts: lead cry:lead@lead lower:strings@lead bass root:bass@bass gallop:bass@bass pad perc hats:perc@perc fx:perc@perc
tempo: 120
meter: 4/4
key: d minor
order: intro rise turn theme open [theme2 theme3] home end

// The ostinato alone - plucked from the first note, as the original is,
// with the synth under it opening - and one held D over it.
section intro bars:8
  bass.figure dyn:mp..mf feel:tight
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
  lead dyn:pp..mp
    | d5:16^ | [d5 f5]:16^ |

// The roots and the choir arrive; the held D becomes D F, then D F A.
section rise bars:12
  bass.figure dyn:mf feel:tight
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
  root dyn:mp
    | d2:16 | a1:16 | bb1:16 |
  pad dyn:p..mp
    | [d3 f3 a3 d4]:16 | [e3 g3 c4]:16 | [d3 f3 bb3]:8 [d3 f3 bb3 d4]:8 |
  lead dyn:mp
    | d5:16 | [d5 f5]:16 | [d5 f5 a5]:16^ |
  fx dyn:p..mp
    | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 | r:4 |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |

// C, and the held chord opens to A C E; then high Bb, the flat sixth,
// over the held chord for a bar - the darkest note in the piece, as the
// pickup. It is the
// original's signature, and it is not played straight: struck hard, bent up
// a whole tone at once, held on the C, then let sag back through the Bb to
// just under it as the melody arrives. The shape is the 1995 file's own
// pitch-wheel moves, read off it and written out in beats. Strings cannot
// bend, so it is Keen alone, the lead's crying synth voice.
section turn bars:4
  bass.figure dyn:mf feel:tight
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
  root dyn:mp
    | c2:16 |
  pad dyn:mp
    | [e3 a3 c4]:8 [e3 a3 c4 e4]:8 |
  lead.hold dyn:mp..mf
    | [a4 c5 e5]:16 |
  cry dyn:f bend:+200@0.4,+200@2,0@3.56,-40@3.9
    | r:12 bb5:4! |
  fx dyn:mp
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |
    | shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25! shaker:0.25. shaker:0.25 shaker:0.25. |

// The second and third statements' rhythm section, as the original has it.
// A root gallops for four bars; the kit plays a backbeat and fills every
// fourth bar, with a longer fill at the end of a phrase.
pattern trot
  | d2:0.5 d2:0.25*2 d2:0.5 d2:0.25*2 d2:0.5 d2:0.25*2 d2:0.5 d2:0.25*2 |
pattern beat_feet
  | kick:2! kick:2 |
pattern beat_hands
  | r:1 snare:1! r:1 snare:1! |
pattern fill_feet
  | kick:2! kick:1 kick:1 |
pattern fill_hands
  | r:1 snare:1.25! snare:0.5 snare:0.75 snare:0.25 snare:0.25! |
pattern roll_feet
  | kick:2! kick:0.5 kick:0.5 kick:1 |
pattern roll_hands
  | r:1 snare:1.25! snare:0.5 snare:0.5 snare:0.25 snare:0.25 snare:0.25! |
// The hats as the original plays them: a texture under the backbeat, not
// beside it - the loudest of them two thirds of a snare. The closed hat
// leans on each beat, the open hat falls on the third, sixth, tenth,
// thirteenth and fifteenth sixteenths. `hats_in` is their first two bars,
// before the last two opens arrive.
pattern hats
  | hat:0.25! hat:0.25. hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25! hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25! hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25. hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. |
pattern hats_in
  | hat:0.25! hat:0.25. hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25! hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25! hat_open:0.25 hat:0.25. hat:0.25. hat:0.25! hat:0.25. hat:0.25 hat:0.25. |

// The melody: two voices a third apart, a whole note a bar. No drums yet
// but the shaker, and the hats coming in over the last two bars.
section theme bars:16
  bass.figure dyn:mf feel:tight
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 |
    | d1:0.25! a1:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 a1:0.25 f1:0.25 g1:0.25 a1:0.25 c2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 f2:0.25 e2:0.25 d2:0.25 c2:0.25 |
  root dyn:mf
    | d2:16 | a1:16 | bb1:16 | c2:16 |
  pad dyn:mp
    | [d3 f3 a3 d4]:16 | [e3 g3 c4]:16 |
    | [d3 f3 bb3]:16 | [e3 a3 c4]:16 |
  // The melody is played, not held. Same notes, same one-a-bar pulse the
  // original has - what changes is the bow. `^` swells a note under its
  // written level, up past it, and back before it releases, which the
  // strings can only do now that they are sent expression instead of the
  // mod wheel; see the layer controls in wayfarer.json. Not every bar
  // swells. A section that swelled on all sixteen would be as mechanical as
  // one that never did, so the bow moves on the notes a phrase arrives at
  // and rests on the notes between, and each four-bar phrase dies away on
  // its last. Bar 9's A is the high point of the section and the only note
  // taken with the bow already moving. The two voices sit behind the beat
  // and not by the same amount - the inner part leans later still, because
  // a section that speaks in perfect unison is one instrument rather than a
  // desk of players. The first note is the exception to the bow: it is taken
  // at level, because it answers the Bb and a swell from under it reads as
  // a gap.
  lead.upper dyn:mp..mf art:sustain feel:loose pocket:lay
